          "id": "doc-ca3c249b3f5f::sentence-4",
          "documentId": "doc-ca3c249b3f5f",
          "text": "Thereafter, Sweden joined the Alliance on 7 March 2024, after Sweden’s Accession Protocol was ratified by all NATO member countries according to their national procedures and its Instrument of Accession was deposited with the US State Department.\n",
          "start": 630,
          "end": 877,
          "contextSpans": [],
          "context": "Thereafter, Sweden joined the Alliance on 7 March 2024, after Sweden’s Accession Protocol was ratified by all NATO member countries according to their national procedures and its Instrument of Accession was deposited with the US State Department."
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-ca3c249b3f5f::sentence-3",
          "documentId": "doc-ca3c249b3f5f",
          "text": "Subsequently, Finland acceded to the Washington Treaty (or the North Atlantic Treaty) when the country (represented by the Finnish Foreign Minister) deposited its Instrument of Accession with the United States government (represented by the US Secretary of State) at NATO Headquarters, making Finland a full member of the Alliance on 4 April 2023.\n",
          "start": 282,
          "end": 630,
          "contextSpans": [],
          "context": "Subsequently, Finland acceded to the Washington Treaty (or the North Atlantic Treaty) when the country (represented by the Finnish Foreign Minister) deposited its Instrument of Accession with the United States government (represented by the US Secretary of State) at NATO Headquarters, making Finland a full member of the Alliance on 4 April 2023."
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-7a01f78ccd01::sentence-5",
          "documentId": "doc-7a01f78ccd01",
          "text": "NATO Secretary General Jens Stoltenberg said: “This is a historic day. Sweden will now take its rightful place at NATO’s table, with an equal say in shaping NATO policies and decisions. After over 200 years of non-alignment Sweden now enjoys the protection granted under Article 5, the ultimate guarantee of Allies’ freedom and security. Sweden brings with it capable armed forces and a first-class defence industry. Sweden’s accession makes NATO stronger, Sweden safer and the whole Alliance more secure. Today’s accession demonstrates that NATO’s door remains open and that every nation has the right to choose its own path.”",
          "start": 366,
          "end": 993,
          "contextSpans": [
            {
              "id": "doc-7a01f78ccd01::sentence-4",
              "documentId": "doc-7a01f78ccd01",
              "text": "With Sweden’s accession, NATO now counts 32 countries among its members.\n",
              "start": 293,
              "end": 366,
              "direction": "PREVIOUS"
            }
          ],
          "context": "With Sweden’s accession, NATO now counts 32 countries among its members. NATO Secretary General Jens Stoltenberg said: “This is a historic day. Sweden will now take its rightful place at NATO’s table, with an equal say in shaping NATO policies and decisions. After over 200 years of non-alignment Sweden now enjoys the protection granted under Article 5, the ultimate guarantee of Allies’ freedom and security. Sweden brings with it capable armed forces and a first-class defence industry. Sweden’s accession makes NATO stronger, Sweden safer and the whole Alliance more secure. Today’s accession demonstrates that NATO’s door remains open and that every nation has the right to choose its own path.”"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-7a01f78ccd01::sentence-3",
          "documentId": "doc-7a01f78ccd01",
          "text": "Sweden became NATO’s newest member on Thursday (7 March 2024), upon depositing its instrument of accession to the North Atlantic Treaty with the Government of the United States in Washington DC. ",
          "start": 98,
          "end": 293,
          "contextSpans": [],
          "context": "Sweden became NATO’s newest member on Thursday (7 March 2024), upon depositing its instrument of accession to the North Atlantic Treaty with the Government of the United States in Washington DC."
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-7a01f78ccd01::sentence-4",
          "documentId": "doc-7a01f78ccd01",
          "text": "With Sweden’s accession, NATO now counts 32 countries among its members.\n",
          "start": 293,
          "end": 366,
          "contextSpans": [],
          "context": "With Sweden’s accession, NATO now counts 32 countries among its members."
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-ca3c249b3f5f::sentence-5",
          "documentId": "doc-ca3c249b3f5f",
          "text": "Finland's cooperation with NATO as a partner was mutually beneficial and included the following activities, many of which it continues to participate in as an Ally:",
          "start": 877,
          "end": 1041,
          "contextSpans": [
            {
              "id": "doc-ca3c249b3f5f::sentence-4",
              "documentId": "doc-ca3c249b3f5f",
              "text": "Thereafter, Sweden joined the Alliance on 7 March 2024, after Sweden’s Accession Protocol was ratified by all NATO member countries according to their national procedures and its Instrument of Accession was deposited with the US State Department.\n",
              "start": 630,
